<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="section-cream">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header reveal">
      <h2>What homeowners ask before they call.</h2>
      <div class="ornament"><div class="ornament-line"></div><div class="ornament-diamond"></div><div class="ornament-line"></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">So what's the catch?</button><div class="faq-a">The parts of a cabinet you'll never see, like the box, the joints and how the hardware mounts, are built one proven way instead of being reinvented for every kitchen. It's the same way a custom home is built from standard 2x4s. Everything you do see is made to your sizes and choices.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">How can custom cabinets cost half of what a custom shop charges?</button><div class="faq-a">We removed the costs that don't make your cabinets better: big-city factory overhead, a showroom, hours of manual drafting and quoting, and warehouses of inventory. Your cabinets are built by an experienced Prairie manufacturing partner, our software handles most of the design and ordering work, and every part is cut only after you approve your design.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">Are the cabinets really built to my measurements?</button><div class="faq-a">Yes. Cabinet widths, heights and depths are made to your kitchen, not rounded to the nearest catalogue size. That means no gaps covered with trim, and a layout planned around your space.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">What are the cabinets made of?</button><div class="faq-a">Cabinet boxes are high-quality particleboard that resists warping and splitting. Sink cabinets and toe kicks, where water is most likely, use plywood. Edge banding is fused into the panel, so edges are watertight and resist swelling. Melamine finishes are from Tafisa.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">What door styles and finishes can I choose?</button><div class="faq-a">Most kitchens use slab, shaker, slim shaker or shaker with a detailed inside profile, in painted, solid wood or melamine finishes. If you have something else in mind, like raised panel or handleless, ask us. We can do that too.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">Where do I see the finishes?</button><div class="faq-a">Instead of driving to a showroom, we bring real door and finish samples to your home. You see them in your own light, next to your floors and counters.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">How much does a kitchen cost?</button><div class="faq-a">Most kitchen projects start around $10,000. Your price depends on the size, layout, door style and finishes. In your first design meeting, we design your kitchen and show you what it would cost.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">What happens in the first design meeting?</button><div class="faq-a">We look at your space and talk through how you want it to work. Then we design your kitchen together, with your actual selections. You leave with photorealistic images of how it could look and a price for the project.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">Do you install the cabinets?</button><div class="faq-a">Installation is optional. Your cabinets arrive assembled, and we can arrange installation through our trusted installation partners, or you can use your own installer.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">How long does it take?</button><div class="faq-a">Production takes four to six weeks from the date your design is signed off and paid. We confirm your timeline before you order.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">What warranty is included?</button><div class="faq-a">Your cabinetry comes with a 10-year warranty. We'll walk you through the coverage when you review your project.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">I'm a designer or contractor. Can I work with you?</button><div class="faq-a">Yes. We can design and price your client's cabinets in one meeting, share drawings and renderings, and coordinate delivery with your schedule. Homeowners are welcome to bring their designer or contractor too.</div></div>
      <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" type="button">Do you work outside Winnipeg?</button><div class="faq-a">We currently serve Winnipeg and the surrounding area. If you're nearby, mention it when you book and we'll let you know if we can help.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

